{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten","id":912563,"title":"Waking Nightmares (or) On the nature and process of becoming Begotten.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-11T18:33:21-07:00","id":912563,"title":"Waking Nightmares (or) On the nature and process of becoming Begotten.","content":"I listened to a podcast very recently that critically examined Beast: the Primordial, and while they made some very good points that I had taken for granted before the biggest thing I took away from it was a great deal of confusion surrounding what a Beast is and the nature of their transformation.<br /> <br /> When a Beast is devoured do they cease to be human immediately? Or, does one remain virtually the same with the exception of the Horror now residing within both your subconscious mind and soul? Is there a timeframe for which Beast must struggle trough accepting what they are and what they've become? Or does the Devouring bring an immediate sense of purpose and acceptance with one's condition? What about a Beast's Touchstones? I know I read at some point in the book that Beasts have them to remind them of their human halves, but no real rules exist and no examples are given. <br /> <br /> Is any of this ever explained in the book? Or was this purposely left up to ST and player creativity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellchecking 06-12-2016, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T18:41:25-07:00","id":912565,"title":"","content":"Having human Touchstones kind of goes against the theme of finding your true Kin among the other supernaturals. The game was built from the ground up for that. Beasts do have their Life trait along with Legend, and nothing explicitly prevents them from having human True Friends (which grant 1 willpower point in a scene of interaction). <br /> <br /> That being said, I agree that the process of becoming a Beast could be clearer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T19:08:56-07:00","id":912572,"title":"","content":"A Beast equivalent of Wolf-Blooded or Sleepwalkers would be delightful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T19:21:52-07:00","id":912577,"title":"","content":"The Restless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T19:44:35-07:00","id":912591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912565#post912565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(. . . )That being said, I agree that the process of becoming a Beast could be clearer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That . . . would be contentious. In the original draft, it was clear - you were always a Beast, you just didn't know it yet (hence the terms &quot;Homecoming&quot; and &quot;Soul&quot;). In the final draft, (what with &quot;Devouring&quot;) its sounds more like its something that happens to you. Arguments over which was better have raged ever since.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Isn't it great? The original release isn't even out yet, but we already have edition wars . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T20:43:08-07:00","id":912610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912577#post912577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Restless?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it weren't for Mage being all over the term, Sleepwalker would be great. Something like The Waking, maybe? Someone who touches the Primordial Dream fitfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T20:53:17-07:00","id":912615,"title":"","content":"Well see, here's the thing. (And the main reason why I posted this discussion thread.)<br /> <br /> All Chronicle of Darkness gamelines revolve around exploring one's humanity to some varying degree.<br /> <br /> Vampire is arguably about defining one's humanity in the face of eternal damnation.<br /> <br /> Werewolf about balancing one's human half with the wolf spirit within. <br /> <br /> Mage about seeking apotheosis beyond humanity without losing their own humanity. <br /> <br /> Promethean about defining and discovering what it means to be human. <br /> <br /> Changeling about losing human innocence and searching for meaning despite such trauma.<br /> <br /> Geist about never taking one's human life for granted when one's been given a second chance.<br /> <br /> Mummy about uncovering lost humanity in the face of inevitable dissolution. <br /> <br /> And Demon, freak'n God Machine Angel Demon the Descent is about what happens when an automaton gains humanity and the burned of such a gift/curse.<br /> <br /> If Beasts is truly about abandoning humanity, or at the very least discovering one's monstrosity then why on earth would another supernatural splat ever want to associate with these inhuman creatures except under specific circumstances. (Circle of the Crone, the Pure, Seers, Centimany, Loyalists, Abmortals, Shank-Sen [butchered that name - . -'] respectively) How can a player connect with a truly inhuman being? Is that truly the point? Is there no room for such stories in Beast the Primordial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T21:10:04-07:00","id":912628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912615#post912615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Beasts is truly about abandoning humanity, or at the very least discovering one's monstrosity then why on earth would another supernatural splat ever want to associate with these inhuman creatures except under specific circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;very specific circumstances&quot; you're talking about are &quot;something that was raised human but understands the realities of supernatural hungers with an immediacy few other monsters can match believes it can see some of itself in you and wants to cultivate/curate/commiserate with your personal and/or magical qualities in part due to that sympathy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lower Lair and higher Satiety let the younger Children blend in easier in part because they're not so hungry that they spoil the good impression Thicker Than Water gives with the more predictable fallout of feeding. Your list of specific example monsters has more staying power among elder Beasts in part because the most common ground of Kinship comes more to the fore for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T22:16:59-07:00","id":912645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912572#post912572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Beast equivalent of Wolf-Blooded or Sleepwalkers would be delightful.</div> </div> </div> </div>There arguably already is one. It's just that, unlike Sleepwalkers and the Wolf-Blooded, the default relationship between Beasts and their \u201clesser template\u201d mortal counterparts is antagonistic.<br /> <br /> (No power stat; still use Integrity; draw their powers from the same source that Beasts draw <i>their</i> powers from.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T23:26:25-07:00","id":912660,"title":"","content":"I must admit, this is very disheartening. <br /> <br /> From what I've read so far it seems that the Devouring just strips a person of their conscience and human attachment immediately upon it's completion. There's no easy way to say this, but the only other parallel I can think of from another gameline is the creation and replacement of a mortal stolen by the True Fae by their Fetch. And even then it often ends up that the Fetch doesn't even realize it's an imposter until their Changeling returns to earth and must then come to grips with what they really are. <br /> <br /> Am I really reading into this correctly? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T00:52:27-07:00","id":912683,"title":"","content":"Not exactly. The Devouring subsumes the person and the end result is something not entirely the original, but not wholly alien. A few people have described the Horror as very much an Id type of being. That seems to fit for my reading of it. <br /> <br /> Your soul is subsumed by the Horror and integrated into it, causing the Horror to exist in the material world as your unrestrained impulse and desires. It causes the human mind to exist in the Primordial Dream as a higher/guiding conscious to the monster that is the Horror. To quote many a fused monster in Persona &quot;I am thou. Thou art I.&quot; I would honestly compare it more to a mage's awakening. It isn't that it rewrites how you handle things, but it gives you a new view to look at the world which may cause you to view things differently. I mean the world is going to look slightly different from a normal human that gets a thrill out of proving themselves the best at a sport, vs a person that has a voice in the back of their mind demanding that competition should not result in you just winning it should end with you grinding your opponent into the dirt to show just how much better you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T00:56:26-07:00","id":912685,"title":"","content":"Got a link to that podcast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T01:05:26-07:00","id":912688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912660#post912660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit, this is very disheartening. <br /> <br /> From what I've read so far it seems that the Devouring just strips a person of their conscience and human attachment immediately upon it's completion. There's no easy way to say this, but the only other parallel I can think of from another gameline is the creation and replacement of a mortal stolen by the True Fae by their Fetch. And even then it often ends up that the Fetch doesn't even realize it's an imposter until their Changeling returns to earth and must then come to grips with what they really are. <br /> <br /> Am I really reading into this correctly? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understand it, the Devouring doesn't so strip you of conscience and attachment as add something else to the mix. Like if you add water to a preexisting solution, the components of the solution will be more diluted than before. Devouring doesn't remove your humanity, it makes it half of a whole where before it was everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T02:25:22-07:00","id":912704,"title":"","content":"Ok, now I'm kinda getting mixed messages. <br /> <br /> My original interpretation of the Devouring is pretty much as you both described nalak42 &amp; ajf115. However, several other interpretations of the Devouring seem to focus around the Horror extinguishing the humanity within the host and replacing it with both the hunger and deeper understanding of the Primordial Dream. Perhaps rephrasing the question will help grant some clarity into this topic. <br /> <br /> During the Devouring, what does the human dreamer loose and gain from the merger? <br /> <br /> P.S. The Kings Raven, the podcast I listened to was Darker Days Radio #72. The hosts were obviously frustrated with the subtext of Beast and while they did obviously misread several parts (the Namtaru review in particularly is hilarious) they did also make some very valid points in regards to the contradictory nature of some of Beast's rules and the lack of refinement that's apparent from the product having to be revised before it was even finished. They have a YouTube channel but I don't think they've released #72 into it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":". 06-12-2016, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T02:46:44-07:00","id":912706,"title":"","content":"Beasts don't have breaking points, and they don't have Integrity. This means that nothing they ever do will rattle them the same way breaking points do a human being.<br /> <br /> I run (and play) that to mean that, yes, their human 'conscience' is instantly destroyed. That said, these beings still had human upbringings, and they still have rationality. They know that killing someone is 'wrong' in our society, even if it doesn't feel 'wrong' to them. The degree to which any given Beast is going to cling to 'humanity' is going to be variable, based on their cultural attachment, social ties, how pragmatic it is to cling to, and how hungry they are.<br /> <br /> They aren't objectively evil. Many are probably really uncomfortable with acts that used to be breaking points for them as a human - they're going to have cognitive dissonance. <br /> <br /> But they aren't breaking points now, and the Hunger is what drives them, in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T03:03:18-07:00","id":912710,"title":"","content":"Alright, I think we're really getting to the crux of the matter now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you all for the input thus far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T03:15:12-07:00","id":912712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912565#post912565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having human Touchstones kind of goes against the theme of finding your true Kin among the other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit off topic but I feel the Game would have benefited from expanding on the subject. Including Mortal relationships could enhance the contrast between the Life and Legend of the Beast, giving each its unique flavor. Also, the Beast attempting to reconcile its new nature with their old life allows for many intense stories. Being rejected or accepted by their human family would shape the Beast's character and inform their relationship with the supernatural. As things stand now, their Lives stand separate and mostly ignored. I've heard complaints that even though Beast is designed for crossover it has too little of its own personality to make it worthwhile. I feel that expanding on Mortal-Beast relationships is one of the ways to remedy that. That's why I respect what Christine Beard did in &quot;It Gets Easier&quot; from Beast Anthology. The story ends tragically, but it dared to address the subject.<br /> <br /> I also think that Chambers should be generated by all Integrity loss, not just that caused by the supernatural. Beasts would feel attracted to places representing the worst humanity has to offer, which is excellent story material. It even enhances the present Lesson-teaching philosophy, by pointing out where the Beast might want to get involved. More than that, I think it's an organic way to make even amoral Beasts look better. &quot;Sure&quot; a Beast says, &quot;I'm an abomination, but the world that allows this to happen can also have a place for me&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T04:01:08-07:00","id":916764,"title":"","content":"Alright, I think I have a suitable answer to my original inquiry. Plus there are mechanical implications and examples from other gamelines that back this idea up:<br /> <br /> Beast's don't immediately lose their humanity or morality, but the higher their Lair rating goes the less human they both feel and become.<br /> <br /> 1. The higher a Beast's Lair becomes the more often they have to feed, thus they would have to become accustom to inhumanity to some varying degree.<br /> <br /> 2. The Shock that all Beasts feed off of doesn't always come from a Breaking Point, although all Breaking Points generate the Shock, but Chambers in a Lair almost exclusively come from locations where mortal or supernatural souls were shedder by trauma. Thus the higher a Beast's Lair, the more nightmarish they become on the inside both literally and figuratively.<br /> <br /> 3. All other gamelines, with the exception of Demon and maybe Promethean express the supernatural's power rating as an indicator for how far away from humans they've become. Especially in the instance of Changeling the Lost, where high Wyrd is almost feared by Changeling society at large because of how close the the Gentry they're becoming.<br /> <br /> And that's all I've got for now. How does that sound everyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T12:34:06-07:00","id":916943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=916764#post916764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's all I've got for now. How does that sound everyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty well-gotten. Main additions:<br /> <br /> 1. It's not so much that powerful Beasts have to feed more often as it is that they get hungry more quickly, which, combined with the effects of Lair on two of the three main Satiety Conditions and Inflicting Nightmares, tends to skew older Beasts toward the end of the Satiety scale on which they are primarily motivated by their Hunger.<br /> <br /> 2. This is primarily true of the Chambers in hives; true to form, Nightmares serve the Kinship-weighted side of the game by being usable with a delayed effect for more subtle expansion of the Dream.<br /> <br /> 3. Even Demon and Promethean \u2014 the commonality of interplay between Supernatural Tolerance and Integrity-analogs are such that high-Azoth Prometheans have a harder time as their Pilgrimage nears its end, and high-Primum demons are increasingly incentivized to use the method of Cover-building that destroys a soul (between the innate higher rating, the capacity to retain multiple identities, and the existence of persistent Cover-threatening glitches) rather than the secure but slow-building method of living a human life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}